  "caption": "Quinn's wet footprint showed just a heel and toes, and the same ankle kept rolling.\n\nA rigid high arch doesn't flatten much under load, so it can absorb less shock and pile pressure onto the heel and ball of the foot. Arch shape can play a part, but it's rarely the whole story.\n\nWhat often helps: stable shoes with a roomy toe box and firm heel, asking about custom insoles rather than generic arch pushers, balance and outer-ankle strength work, and properly finishing rehab after any sprain.\n\nIf only one foot has a high arch, the arch is getting higher, or you notice numb feet, tripping or weaker legs, see your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
